# Android (`apps/android`)

- `:domain` is pure JVM Kotlin (no Android SDK). Put entities, ports, and sync helpers there so `./gradlew :domain:test` runs in CI.
- `:app` has `data` (Retrofit, Room, NSD, WorkManager, FileProvider) and `presentation` (Compose + ViewModels).
- ViewModels depend on use-case interfaces. Hilt binds implementations.
- mDNS service type: `_mydrive._tcp`.
- After LAN login the client downloads the sync manifest, stores files under `filesDir/media`, and browses them offline.
- In-app updates: `GET /v1/app/releases/latest` vs `BuildConfig.VERSION_CODE`, then install the APK from the backoffice catalog.
- App version comes from git: last semver tag on the branch (`1.0.0` / `v1.0.0`) plus patch per commit after it; no tags → `0.0.N` from commit count. `versionCode` is that commit count. Do not hardcode `versionName` / `versionCode` in `app/build.gradle.kts`.
- Compile the APK with `./gradlew :app:assembleRelease` (CI job `android-apk`).
